 { Black is a pawn down, and there is another one in danger on b6. } 1... { -KEY- } Rd2 $1 { Seizing the second rank, which doesn't just help Black to attack the enemy pawns, it also enhances his future counterplay on the kingside. } ( { In contrast, passive defence with } 1... Rd6 $6 { is strongly met by } 2. Ke2 Kf6 3. a4 $1 Ke5 4. a5 bxa5 5. Rxa5 Kf4 6. b4 { with the plan of Ra3-b3 and b4-b5. } ) 
