Rc2 5. a5 f3 6. a6 Re2 7. Kd1 e3 $1 ( 7. Ke1 Rxf2 { surprisingly fails to } 8. a7 Rf1 9. Kd2 Ra1 10. Rb7 Kg6 11. Ke3 { etc. } ) 
8. fxe3 Rxe3 { I guess that in practice, White still has some work left to do. } ) 
Rc2 4. Rb5 Kg4 $1 5. h3+ ( { White opts for pawn exchanges, seeing that } 5. a4 $6 f4 { with ...Kf3 next, would even be dangerous for him. } ) 
